---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Reclaiming Hours Lost to the Supplier Email Cycle - Marker">
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-16 md:pt-24 md:pb-24">
      <a
        href="/case-studies"
        class="mb-8 inline-flex items-center text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground"
      >
        <svg
          class="mr-1 h-4 w-4"
          fill="none"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
        >
          <path
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
        </svg>
        All Case Studies
      </a>

      <span
        class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-primary"
      >
        Premium Menswear
      </span>
      <h1
        class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl"
      >
        Reclaiming Hours Lost to the Supplier Email Cycle
      </h1>

      <div
        class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 p-5 text-sm"
      >
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Company</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground"
              >Premium menswear brand, DTC + wholesale</span
            >
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Team</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground"
              >~12-person product development team; fewer than 12 suppliers</span
            >
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Key Challenge</span
            >
            <span class="text-muted-foreground"
              >Email overload consuming productive hours; no internal
              collaboration layer before responding to suppliers</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Challenge</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          The VP of Product Development at this premium menswear brand described
          the daily reality facing his team: merchants handling 70 to 80 emails
          per day, with roughly half requiring them to pull files from other
          systems, check tech packs, or cross-reference purchase orders before
          they could respond. The VP himself was spending an estimated four hours
          a day in email.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          He called it the "evil email cycle" — a pattern where every supplier
          message triggers a cascade of internal lookups, side conversations, and
          delayed responses. There was no way to discuss a supplier email
          internally before sending a reply. Team members often weren't sure who
          should respond to which messages, and things would get stuck when the
          right person didn't see a thread in time.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          When a ship date changed, for example, the update needed to reach
          logistics, merchants, and marketing — but there was no automated way to
          cascade that notification. The team was manually tracking these
          dependencies, often through yet more email.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Approach</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          Marker connects to the team's existing supplier email workflow and
          provides an internal collaboration layer on top of it. Rather than
          replacing email, Marker captures the communication stream and gives the
          team tools to discuss, assign, and validate before responses go out.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          When a supplier sends an email — for instance, notifying of a ship date
          delay — Marker surfaces contextual information alongside the message:
          the relevant purchase order, penalty clauses, and the downstream teams
          that need to be informed. Team members can tag colleagues, draft
          responses collaboratively, and assign follow-up actions without leaving
          the platform.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          Marker also validates incoming supplier communications against existing
          agreements. If a rate card isn't being followed or a ship date change
          conflicts with contractual terms, the team is alerted before they
          respond. For this brand, where margins are strong and relationships with
          long-tenured vendors run deep, this validation layer protects the
          business without requiring adversarial negotiations.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">Key Takeaways</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-muted-foreground">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Internal collaboration on supplier emails before responses are
              sent, reducing back-and-forth and miscommunication</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Automatic validation of supplier communications against rate
              cards and contractual terms</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Cascading notifications when ship dates or PO details change,
              ensuring logistics, merchants, and marketing stay aligned</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Clear assignment of email ownership, preventing threads from
              stalling when the right person doesn't see them</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Dashboard-level visibility into team communication patterns with
              suppliers, surfacing bottlenecks</span
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section
        class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-6 text-center"
      >
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-foreground">
          See how Marker can help your team reclaim hours lost to supplier email.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/book-demo"
          class="mt-4 inline-flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary px-6 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary/90 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2"
        >
          Book a Demo
        </a>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
